# ── Trusted-proxy client-IP resolution ───────────────────────────────
#
# QuickScale supports canonical client-IP resolution behind a trusted
# reverse proxy (e.g. Railway edge, Cloudflare, or an application-layer
# proxy).  Both settings are environment-configurable so that single-host
# (no-proxy) deployments keep ``REMOTE_ADDR`` with no configuration
# change required.
#
# - ``USE_X_FORWARDED_FOR`` (default ``False``): when enabled, the
#   application reads the ``X-Forwarded-For`` header to determine the
#   real client IP instead of ``REMOTE_ADDR``.
# - ``TRUSTED_PROXY_COUNT`` (default ``0``): the number of trusted
#   reverse proxies in front of the application.  The client IP is
#   extracted at position ``-TRUSTED_PROXY_COUNT`` (the Nth entry from
#   the right) in the ``X-Forwarded-For`` chain.
#
# ``quickscale_core.runtime.settings.ClientIdentityMiddleware`` validates these
# settings and normalizes X-Forwarded-For before every request consumer. The
# live ``quickscale_modules_orgs.current_org.get_client_ip`` resolver and DRF's
# ``NUM_PROXIES`` path therefore observe the same fail-closed forwarding state.

